// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row refbind_byvalue_struct_field_read_wrong (tier 1, `run 1`).
// FOUND 2026-09-09f while varying the SHAPE of the ref-binder hand programs, and it is
// NOT a segfault — it is a SILENT WRONG ANSWER, which is the reason it is filed apart
// from the two `ref`-over-a-reference rows. Neither arm that fixes those moves it
// (`tlrbspill`/`tlrbspillx`: still 1); an arm that only carries the aggregate SHAPE
// (`tlrbshape`) moves it to 0 and moves nothing else. MEASURED on 0158e823a73f6ba1 43.
//
// `match s { ref w => w.a }` over a BY-VALUE struct. Here the match door's alias
// branch is RIGHT — `scrut` is the struct's address, so `w : &S` is that pointer —
// but the binding is registered with `var_elem_types_[w] = ptr` and NO `var_struct_`
// shape, so `w.a` GEPs through the alloca wrap and reads the pointer's own bytes as
// field `a`. `src/compiler/mlir_gen_stmt.cpp::pat_bind`'s RefBind case already carries
// the shape for exactly this reason (its comment names the same silent miscompile);
// `gen_match`'s top-level copy does not.
//
// THE SHAPE IS STRUCT-ONLY AND READ-THROUGH-THE-BINDER-ONLY, both measured on the same
// binary: the by-value TUPLE twin `match t { ref w => w.0 }` exits 0, and
// `match s { ref w => { let q: &S = w; q.a } }` exits 0. Census over all 6602 registered
// pass fixtures: the by-value-aggregate arrival count at this door is ZERO, so this
// program is the door's only carrier anywhere in the tree.
//
// The oracle is an EXIT CODE: 0 when `w.a` reads the 4 that is there, 1 today.
package refbind_byvalue_struct_field_read_wrong;
struct S { pub a: i64 }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let s: S = S{ a: 4i64 };
    match s {
        ref w => {
            if w.a != 4i64 { return 1i32; }
            return 0i32;
        }
    }
}
